00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.840
So now to the next presentation,

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.790
and here the one thing
that I wanna point out

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:22.600
is how too much graphical things,

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.560
how too many animations
can really take away

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.730
from the content of the slides

00:11:27.730 --> 00:11:30.530
and can even also look
unprofessional to some extent.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:33.400
So here if you go over there
are so many animations,

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:36.780
so many colors that do not really add much

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:39.040
to the actual content
with the actual meaning.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.450
That the things that you actually
wanna say with your slides

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:43.180
get completely diminished.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.940
So here just be sure that
you use graphical elements

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:50.080
like this and bold colors
like this very selectively

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:54.200
usually less is more, and
the same is true animations.

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:57.010
Usually there are no animations
and presentations like this.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.730
One of the reasons being that often

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.400
these presentations are
not even getting presented,

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.780
but they're just printed out as documents.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.230
And then you just go over
these documents in a meeting

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:07.920
and everybody just has a handout

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.800
of this presentation document
in front of him or her.

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.380
But even if you are
presenting it on a display,

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:16.240
animations is just not the look fear

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:19.090
that you should go for
four C level presentations.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:21.430
It will be perceived as unprofessional.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.240
This is just not what is expected

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.480
from you in these environments.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:25.640
So now next one and again

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.590
this seems to be from
a university project.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:28.710
And the reason why I included this

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.160
is just because I wanted to show

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.480
you the bit different type of style,

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.300
that this presentation is using.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:36.080
This is a presentation style

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.410
that you will see more
frequently in banking.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.650
So in most consulting context,

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:44.780
pages like that would never
go into the main deck.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.530
It just far too much texts,

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.010
things like this would go in the backup

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.140
but for whatever reason bank has just like

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.840
to put even more words

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.710
in the presentations than consultance,

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.680
but this is indeed what you
will find a if you join a bank.

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:00.040
And just wanna also make you
aware of one other speciality

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.960
that you'll often find in
these banking presentations.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.110
And this is the so-called
footboy fear chart.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:07.740
And this is exactly what you see here,

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.210
bankers use this all the time to display

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:12.550
spreads and company valuations coming

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.060
from different valuation types.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.750
Well, the problem is nobody

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:17.810
understands this outside of banking.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.160
I tried to make charts
like this several time

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.360
in a consulting context.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.840
And I've yet to meet a client

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:27.000
that can understand and
read this type of chart.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.890
So my takeaway here is that
there are some differences

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.720
in consulting compared
to banking presentations,

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.720
though I would argue if you wanna learn

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:35.980
the presentation style,

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:39.200
that will make you successful
in C-level environments

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.120
in boardroom environments
of large corporate firms,

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.743
then I would argue that the
conservative style probably

00:13:44.743 --> 00:13:46.940
will be a bit more successful for you.

00:13:46.940 --> 00:13:49.950
This is at least from my
experience what works much better

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:53.290
if you wanna communicate your
insights to your leadership

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.840
in most business situations
and environments.

